// The site as a Workers Static Assets project (INCIDENTS #1004). Cloudflare Pages refuses more than 20,000 files in a
// deployment; a Worker with static assets takes up to 100,000 on a paid plan (the account has Workers Paid).
// NOT read by Cloudflare Pages (the file name is not wrangler.jsonc): the Pages project keeps serving the site until
// the owner points the domain at this Worker. Test: `npx wrangler dev --config wrangler.static.jsonc` after a build.
//
// «النشر السريع» (INCIDENTS #1296): site-worker/ runs only for an address with no file (a page saved a moment ago that
// the deployment doesn't have yet). It no longer runs first for the listings and the show and story pages: that was
// ~51,000 Worker requests a day plus ~57,000 to arw-site-bot for the fast-lane list, and the free plan allows 100,000
// in all (INCIDENTS #1476; the site builds on GitHub in ~3 minutes now); every other file is served straight from the assets. It shows a
// page saved a moment ago (arw-site-bot, FAST) only until this deployment has it, never after (site-worker/fast.js).
{
  "name": "arw-site-static",
  "main": "site-worker/index.js",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-11-01",
  "assets": {
    "directory": "./_site",
    "binding": "ASSETS",
    "html_handling": "auto-trailing-slash",
    "not_found_handling": "none"
  },
  "services": [{ "binding": "FAST", "service": "arw-site-bot" }]
}
